<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="V850:LE:32:default">
<!--
    GH-4788: "RH850 branch disasembly not correct"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/4788

    The RH850 (G3KH) Bcond disp17 conditional branch was missing from the V850
    SLEIGH (Special.sinc).  The 4 bytes `f9 07 49 fe` are a `bnc` (Bcond, cond
    code nc = 0x9) with a 17-bit displacement, but with the disp17 table entry
    absent the decoder fell through to the overlapping `ld.hu disp16[reg1],reg2`
    form (which shares op0510=0x3F & word2.bit0=1) and mis-decoded them as
    `ld.hu -0x1b8[r25], r0`.  IDA/Trace32 decode this as a bnc/bnl branch.

    Encoding (RH850 Bcond disp17):
      word1: 00000 011111 D cccc   (op1115/reg2 = 0, op0510 = 0x3F,
                                     bit4 = disp[16] sign, op0003 = cond)
      word2: dddddddddddddddd 1    (bits15:1 = disp[16:1], bit0 marker = 1)
      disp17 = sext((D<<16) | (word2[15:1]<<1)) ; here disp = -0x1b8 = -440.

    Placed at 0x196590 (the issue's key address) the branch target is
      0x196590 + (-440) = 0x1963d8.

    Stage: S1 decode-table (SLEIGH spec-fix, no option).  This testcase asserts
    the FIXED decode (a `bnc` conditional branch to 0x1963d8) and forbids the
    buggy `ld.hu` form.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x196590">
f90749fe
</bytechunk>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>disassemble 0x196590 0x196594</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH4788 #1: disp17 Bcond decodes as bnc to 0x1963d8 (not ld.hu)" min="1" max="1">^0x00196590: bnc +0x1963d8$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH4788 #2: the bytes are no longer mis-decoded as ld.hu" min="0" max="0">ld\.hu</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
